🛠️ Ansible Installation & Configuration on AlmaLinux 2023 (AL2023)

🚀 Steps
1. Update System Packages
   sudo dnf -y update

2. Install EPEL Repository
   sudo dnf install epel-release -y

3. Install Ansible
   sudo dnf install ansible -y

4. Verify Ansible Installation
   ansible --version

🔐 SSH Configuration for Root Login

5. Edit SSH Configuration File
   sudo vi /etc/ssh/sshd_config
   
   Use :set number in vi to see line numbers. Modify these lines:
   Line 40: PermitRootLogin yes
   Line 45: PubkeyAuthentication yes
   Line 65: PasswordAuthentication yes

6. Restart and Check SSH Service
   sudo systemctl restart sshd
   sudo systemctl status sshd

🔑 Setup SSH Authentication for Ansible

7. Set/Change Root Password (for SSH login)
   sudo passwd root
   # Use password: root1234 (or your preferred one)

8.  Generate SSH Key (on control node)
    ssh-keygen -t rsa
    # Press Enter to accept default locations

9. Copy SSH Key to Target Host(s)
   ssh-copy-id root@<private_ip>
   # e.g., ssh-copy-id root@192.168.1.10

🖥️ Configure Ansible Inventory

10. Add Hosts to Ansible Inventory
    sudo vi /etc/ansible/hosts
Example:
 [dev]
192.168.1.10
192.168.1.11

✅ Test Ansible Connectivity

ansible -m ping all


Expected output:
192.168.1.10 | SUCCESS => {
    "changed": false,
    "ping": "pong"
}


